# The Android programs this branch's emulator measurements ran, one APK each, the Android SDK
# command-line tools they were run with, and the WebDAV server the synchronization measurement
# served its database from. Four columns: the file's SHA-256; a name and the file,
# which is where `spikes/storage/android` puts it under the work directory's `dl`; the SHA-256 of
# the certificate that signed it; and where it is downloaded from. The fetch refuses a name with no
# line here and a file whose hash differs, and the APK check refuses an APK that `apksigner`
# reports as signed by any other certificate. Measuring another release adds a line.
#
# The measurement ran Keepass2Android 1.15-r6, KeePassDX 4.5.8 and KeePassDroid 2.7, and the
# command-line tools; their four lines are the ones its own copy of this file kept. The other three
# lines are the further releases `spikes/revocation-merge` pins, from which this file is taken.
#
# Where each value is published. KeePassDX writes an APK's hash into the text of its release, and
# the digest of its signing certificate into its README, under "Package authenticity from GitHub".
# GitHub reports a digest for the Keepass2Android 1.15-r6 asset and for the KeePassDroid 2.7 asset.
# Keepass2Android 1.08d-r5 has no published hash: that line is the hash of the file that arrived.
# No published digest was found for Keepass2Android's or KeePassDroid's signing certificate, so
# those two are what `apksigner` printed for these files, and what they buy is that both
# Keepass2Android releases carry the same certificate and that a later download is held to it.
#
# The line after the APKs is the command-line tools, which the SDK setup fetches and checks itself.
# Its hash is the value on https://developer.android.com/studio, and a ZIP has no signer, hence the
# `-`.
#
# The last line is rclone 1.68.2 for linux-amd64, the WebDAV server of
# `papers/ground/measured-k2a-synchronize.md`. `spikes/storage/android/server/fetch-rclone.sh`
# fetches it into `server/rclone-dl` beside itself rather than under `dl`, and refuses a file whose
# hash is not this line's or not the hash rclone publishes in the `SHA256SUMS` beside the release.
# This line holds that published hash, which the archive the measurement ran matched. A ZIP has no
# signer, hence the `-`.
